<description>&lt;p&gt;Security forces in Kulgam, Jammu and Kashmir, engaged a Lashkar-e-Taiba cell, killing commander Lateef Ahmad Bhat and other attackers while recovering a body and weapon, and have launched intensified search operations. In Manipur, six Naga civilians were finally buried after 187 days, prompting heightened security and the redeployment of over 1,000 CRPF personnel from Chhattisgarh, including the withdrawal of an anti-Naxal battalion for Manipur duties. The CRPF reported gathering vital clues on the Kulgam attackers. The conflict context includes 437 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxQXzlxN3JBcUcwYVlyQXhVcFcwZ3ZqeWUtaTRpcmdkNlBnUkNhMUwtYmQ1SHVRVF90dXVMRTYxQkppSjI1TnItNVpOVEtfdDJOZDI3dTR2NGZMY2RicnVUS1ZoQnlmYlJmWDZvMzlJUEpDMHJFX3ctbVRkTW5pNlRMbTYwSTdOXzZPVWM0b2FaZEJPRVF1Z3RYaTFVS0loN3U2OUEwODFQM3pkeUdoampXVA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kashmir Convener&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxOLUo4cVdNeWMxMmR6T3FDZ0hSbk9ocE03QWtPX01uMzRoc2xCMmhLN1MyNnhDdzM5aW9DRUstdF9PTUtHR2ZLa2JZSk01SWhjWXUxN0F6V1lwbG8yQU9Pd2w1aC1JSVhfQkxHcTUzcHZyRk9DTFpWREFDc1ZuSzYxT2RxOUR4QVZZdm9hWV9NeFRscl9BbEFyM1JqRTg4bWp4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kashmir Life&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxNdi1QQWhGZzZOVzZsUndzNGJ6cFlzbEtGSVd6NERrS012MGdDeXhaOVlIa25TTnV5UG5fVERMcXczMy1pRHZWMlZQQUltSGpmLTJ2NDdXa29wQi1FTDd1MFM4azdDc3lkQ0VGcUF2RXhtTEZCWFFBY0NoRzUxSG9zS3VOcHprTmlQWktJ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Brighter Kashmir&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE16dFQxb21TZktqQzVXQjlNeHhNNlZ0a3RsQmtNVVFtN1dHbUh0NC1COUJCNkU4VWpkOENJamZlSUJIeVF2RFBlYnZKOWFheFNOT19qelFyTnpHTmVtWXVwMFo2anlSTGs5LVdpSHQ2elVBcFdfQnc